WEBVTT

00:11:59.256 --> 00:12:02.301
Because the table was never built
for us in the first place.

00:12:02.843 --> 00:12:04.011
The solution?

00:12:04.052 --> 00:12:06.138
Build better tables.

00:12:06.472 --> 00:12:10.726
(Applause)

00:12:10.726 --> 00:12:14.855
So, allow me to be
your very own IKEA manual.

00:12:15.647 --> 00:12:18.025
I would like to present to you
a set of guidelines

00:12:18.025 --> 00:12:19.902
I very eloquently call:

00:12:19.943 --> 00:12:22.529
“How to Build a Table that Doesn’t Suck”.

00:12:22.529 --> 00:12:23.697
(Laughter)

00:12:23.739 --> 00:12:25.574
I've been told I'm very literal.

00:12:26.158 --> 00:12:28.118
Now, right off the bat, let me tell you,

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:30.579
this assembly is going to take
more than one person